  "steps": [
    "Pound the thick end of each chicken breast so it is an even thickness, then halve into 4 cutlets. Whisk the buttermilk and kimchi brine in a bowl or zip-top bag, add the chicken, and refrigerate 2 to 8 hours.",
    "Make the kimchi mayo: stir the mayonnaise, chopped kimchi and sriracha together. Chill until needed.",
    "Make the slaw: toss both cabbages and the carrot with the mayonnaise, rice vinegar and salt. Chill until needed.",
    "Make the fried garlic: warm the 3 tbsp oil and minced garlic together in a small skillet over medium-low heat, stirring, 3 to 5 min, until the garlic is light golden. Pour into a heatproof bowl right away, since it keeps cooking in the hot oil.",
    "Heat 2 to 3 in of frying oil in a heavy pot or Dutch oven to 360°F. Set a wire rack over a sheet pan.",
    "Whisk the flour, potato starch, gochugaru, garlic powder and salt in a shallow dish. Lift the chicken from the marinade, let the excess drip off, and press into the dredge to coat well.",
    "Fry 2 cutlets at a time about 7 min, flipping once, until deep golden brown and 165°F inside. Drain on the rack.",
    "While the chicken is hot, spoon the fried garlic and some of its oil over each piece.",
    "Build on toasted buns: kimchi mayo, perilla leaves, slaw, chicken, more kimchi mayo, then the top bun."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "The reel shows the method without amounts. Marinade, dredge, frying and sauce amounts here follow published Korean fried chicken sandwich recipes.",
    "No kimchi brine? Stir 1 tbsp gochugaru into the buttermilk instead."
